<title>GERMANY: Sales rise for Linde AG.</title>
<headline>Sales rise for Linde AG.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German plant and engineering group Linde AG said on Tuesday it expected to improve its earnings and sales in 1997 after sales rose 6.4 percent in the first four months of the year.</p>
<p>Outgoing chief executive Hans Meinhardt said in a speech prepared for delivery at a news conference that growth would continue to come from foreign business and the company wanted a stronger position in Europe, South East Asia and the U.S.</p>
<p>The share of foreign business in overall sales would continue to grow, he said.</p>
</text>
